1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,004
Kia ora. This is Liam, in for Bear. Show-tell used to draw every picture. So the

2
00:00:05,024 --> 00:00:09,399
question isn't whether every picture has to be a drawing. It's whether each picture

3
00:00:09,419 --> 00:00:10,341
earns its motion.

4
00:00:10,411 --> 00:00:14,358
Four terms. Show-tell: one picture per beat, and the voice explains. A beat: a

5
00:00:14,378 --> 00:00:18,325
sentence or two of narration, and the picture under it. A card: an interface

6
00:00:18,345 --> 00:00:23,142
picture, like a player, a chart or a search. And on twos: each drawing held for two

7
00:00:23,162 --> 00:00:25,125
frames, the way stop motion is shot.

8
00:00:25,195 --> 00:00:29,892
Show-tell has one rule. Every beat gets one picture, and the voice does the

9
00:00:29,912 --> 00:00:32,250
explaining. The picture shows. The voice tells.

10
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:37,538
Until now, every picture came from one kit of isometric drawings. Cardboard boxes,

11
00:00:37,558 --> 00:00:40,762
dark blocks, flat pages, all in Claude's colours.

12
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:44,856
Now there's a second choice: sixteen stop-motion cards. Same fonts, same colours,

13
00:00:44,876 --> 00:00:50,247
and every card is shot on twos, so each drawing holds for two frames, like paper

14
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,258
under a camera.

15
00:00:51,328 --> 00:00:56,341
Each card is an interface you already know, moving the way it moves on screen. A

16
00:00:56,361 --> 00:01:00,431
player. Search. Tabs. A chart. A stack. A dock. Flowing paths. And more.

17
00:01:00,501 --> 00:01:05,203
The drawings stay the default. A card is optional. You choose, beat by beat, and a

18
00:01:05,223 --> 00:01:08,154
film can be all drawings, all cards, or a mix.

19
00:01:08,224 --> 00:01:12,814
Pick a card when the idea is an interface. A search card types the query, then drops

20
00:01:12,834 --> 00:01:17,696
the results in one at a time, so the voice can say 'you ask, it returns' while it

21
00:01:17,716 --> 00:01:17,967
happens.

22
00:01:18,037 --> 00:01:23,123
Pick one when the idea is a set of numbers. These are the beat lengths of the first

23
00:01:23,143 --> 00:01:27,377
show-tell film, in seconds. The bars grow, then melt into a line: the same numbers,

24
00:01:27,397 --> 00:01:28,228
a different shape.

25
00:01:28,298 --> 00:01:32,895
Or when the idea is a single word. The word fills from below, inside its own

26
00:01:32,915 --> 00:01:35,204
outline, while the voice says what it means.

27
00:01:35,274 --> 00:01:39,836
Under the hood, nothing new. The beat sheet drives the audio, the Manim drawings and

28
00:01:39,856 --> 00:01:42,585
the cards, and all three meet in one master.

29
00:01:42,655 --> 00:01:47,581
And the laws still hold. Labels stay at one to three words. Terracotta is an accent,

30
00:01:47,601 --> 00:01:52,218
never text. Type stays at forty-eight pixels or more. Every card moves on twos, with

31
00:01:52,238 --> 00:01:54,382
a flat paper shadow and no blur.

32
00:01:54,452 --> 00:01:59,049
So mix them. Keep at least two drawn beats. Never put two cards of the same kind

33
00:01:59,069 --> 00:02:02,851
back to back. And choose a card only when its motion is the point.

34
00:02:02,921 --> 00:02:06,377
Your turn. Paste this into Claude: I'm making a 90-second explainer about [your

35
00:02:06,397 --> 00:02:10,655
topic]. Plan it as a show-tell film: one picture per beat, six to ten beats. For

36
00:02:10,675 --> 00:02:14,666
each beat, write the one or two sentences the voice says, then choose the picture:

37
00:02:14,686 --> 00:02:19,212
an isometric drawing, or one card, but only if the idea is an interface, a set of

38
00:02:19,232 --> 00:02:23,223
numbers, or a single word. Say in one line how the picture's motion carries that

39
00:02:23,243 --> 00:02:26,699
beat's claim. Then check two things yourself. Does each picture move with the

40
00:02:26,719 --> 00:02:31,512
sentence it sits under? And is any beat just a slide of words? If it is, draw it

41
00:02:31,532 --> 00:02:31,779
again.

42
00:02:31,849 --> 00:02:36,342
Show-Tell: Drawings and Cards. At Nik Bear Brown.
